id: E14725
trigger_tool: autoreconf|configure
phase: configuration
error_signature: config.status.*already exists|stale generated Makefile.*compiler|autoreconf.*generated outputs
severity: 2
category: autotools, source-snapshot, build-system
match_keywords: config.status, stale Makefile, generated config.h, autoreconf, source snapshot, exact cleanup
title: Snapshot-carried configured outputs must be removed from the temporary source before Autotools regeneration
root_cause: A source snapshot can include host-specific configure outputs alongside authoritative Autotools inputs. A fresh autoreconf or configure in that mixed tree may consume stale config.status, Makefile or config.h, inherit another host's flags, or fail before generating a target-consistent build.
affected_scope: Autotools source snapshots that actually ship configured outputs; require an exact inspected list of ordinary files in the temporary source. Do not delete configure.ac, Makefile.am, config.guess/sub inputs, patches or user worktrees.
verification_cmd: Inspect the release archive file inventory, remove only expected generated outputs from Conan's disposable source copy, then run autoreconf, target configure, make, package and installed-tool consumer.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: exact-generated-output-quarantine
rec_description: Inventory generated versus authoritative source files. Fail if an expected generated output is absent or is a symlink, delete only the exact generated set from the Conan copy before autoreconf, then assert target toolchain flags and installed binary after the clean configure.
rec_verification_increment: >
  Removing stale outputs makes regeneration mandatory, so a developer's
  installed autoreconf/aclocal cannot serve as a release input. Declare the
  published tools and bind their script interpreter/module/data closure.
  Packaged Automake raw entry points need explicit build-host Perl and
  relocated macro/libdir arguments; OHOS cached Perl XS modules must not be
  mixed into the host interpreter. Verify actual regeneration, make check and
  the installed consumer rather than assuming the presence of autoreconf.
rec_command: In build(), remove only the verified generated files from self.source_folder before autoreconf --force --install.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: clean-vpath-build-if-supported
fallback_description: If the project supports a clean out-of-source build, keep its source tree untouched and configure into an empty task-private build directory; still verify no source-tree stale generated headers leak through include search.
fallback_command: Probe project VPATH support and inspect include paths before selecting the clean build directory.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: rm -rf.*source|delete.*Makefile.am|trust.*shipped.*config.status
forbid_1_reason: Broad deletion destroys authoritative inputs, while trusting configured outputs can silently keep a previous host's compiler flags.
forbid_1_consequence: Reproducibility and target-architecture failure.
